// Sound manifest (JSON5).
//
// "files" is the complete list of sound files the game uses, out of the
// thousands under assets/sounds: nothing else is loaded, and a file listed
// here that nothing plays is an error. Paths are relative to "root".
//
// "hooks" ties each action (dungeon.Sound_Kind) to the sounds it can play;
// one is picked at random each time, never the same twice running.
//   volume    0..1, on top of the mixer volumes and distance
//   interval  seconds that must pass before the same action sounds again
//   bus       "sound" (default) or "music": which mixer volume applies
// Every action has to be listed, the Menu_* ones raised by the pause menu
// included. An empty "sounds" list keeps a hook silent.
//
// "music" is the background playlist. The sound packs hold no songs, so the
// tracks are seamless ambient loops of 11 to 19 seconds; each plays
// "repeats" times over before the next takes its place.
{
	"root": "assets/sounds",

	"music": {
		"tracks": ["vampire_castle_1", "void_loop_1", "vampire_castle_2", "eternal_sands", "vampire_castle_3", "void_loop_2"],
		"repeats": 4
	},

	"files": {
